1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:05,088
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,764
[laughs]

3
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,492
[Emilia] <i>I'll make sure</i>
<i>that even the devil himself</i>

4
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:37,120
<i>won't be able to find</i>
<i>or steal your fortune.</i>

5
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:40,290
<i>That's Magbanua!</i>
<i>What are Julio's men doing here?</i>

6
00:00:40,373 --> 00:00:42,625
[Lily] <i>Diego, we can't let the Ardientes</i>

7
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>take Helena's fortune first.</i>

8
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:47,380
[Emilia] <i>It's time to give them</i>
<i>my little surprise.</i>

9
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:48,631
[loud explosion]

10
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:50,717
[Helena] <i>I want you to be my partner.</i>

11
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:55,055
<i>You deal with the politics,</i>
<i>while I run the syndicate.</i>

12
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:57,974
<i>We will be the most powerful</i>
<i>couple in the land.</i>

13
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,685
<i>Papa's men and Colonel Magbanua are here.</i>

14
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:01,811
<i>They tried to raid us.</i>

15
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:02,896
<i>-Ouch!</i>
<i>-You bastard!</i>

16
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:04,606
[Marlon] <i>Lily's with Diego.</i>

17
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:07,817
<i>They said they would take down</i>
<i>all of Red Dragon's businesses.</i>

18
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>They'll try to look</i>
<i>for her hidden wealth too.</i>

19
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,529
<i>Grandma, you shouldn't be angry</i>
<i>with Grandpa.</i>

20
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,573
<i>The one who really wants</i>
<i>to steal your wealth</i>

21
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:16,659
<i>and your remaining businesses</i>
<i>is none other than Lily Cruz.</i>

22
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:21,581
[Julio] <i>If she's able to destroy</i>
<i>your brothel and the armory,</i>

23
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:24,501
<i>the next thing</i>
<i>she'll destroy is your wealth!</i>

24
00:01:24,584 --> 00:01:27,128
[Helena] <i>Lily Cruz can't get that money.</i>

25
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:30,173
<i>If I lose it all, I'll have nothing left.</i>

26
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:31,674
<i>Everything will be lost!</i>

27
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,426
<i>No!</i>

28
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:35,720
[Lily] <i>We've clipped your wings,</i>
<i>Red Dragon.</i>

29
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:37,597
<i>Now you'll crash right into hell.</i>

30
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,224
[Diego] <i>I think someone's tailing us.</i>

31
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:49,067
[somber music playing]

32
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:02,956
Lino.

33
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:06,626
-Are they home yet?
-Not yet, ma'am.

34
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:09,254
I hope you're safe, Lily.

35
00:02:09,921 --> 00:02:10,922
[exhales]

36
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:16,678
-Auntie.
-Anna! Marlon! Come in, quick.

37
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:18,263
Auntie.

38
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,058
-Ma'am.
-Is Lily home yet?

39
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:25,854
That's the problem.
I'm worried sick. She's not home yet.

40
00:02:27,313 --> 00:02:29,440
Oh no. Where could they be?

41
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,777
Did something happen to them?
I hope they're safe.

42
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,988
I know. I'm so worried.

43
00:02:43,621 --> 00:02:46,791
[action music playing]

44
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:26,748
Someone's coming.

45
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:34,464
-Who's that?
-That's Damian.

46
00:03:42,805 --> 00:03:45,225
[panting]

47
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:47,602
Damian!

48
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,687
Damian, what happened to you?

49
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,609
-Are you all right?
-Are you okay?

50
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:57,820
-Hold on, I'll just tend to him.
-I'll help you.

51
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,960
<i>I want to ask for your forgiveness.</i>

52
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,920
<i>Please give me another chance.</i>

53
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:16,130
<i>Anna, talk to me. I'm going crazy here.</i>

54
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:18,716
<i>-There's nothing to talk about.</i>
<i>-Anna, wait.</i>

55
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:43,408
They're not here!

56
00:04:45,076 --> 00:04:46,035
[shushes]

57
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:49,998
[suspenseful music playing]

58
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:55,003
Let's go look for them!

59
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:01,884
Are you okay?

60
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:08,099
[romantic music playing]

61
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:23,906
[romantic music playing]

62
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:48,139
[romantic music playing]

63
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:09,744
Diego. Diego.

64
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:14,957
Just a little longer…

65
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,086
and we'll finally be free.

66
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:21,923
We can finally be together.

67
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,009
Just a little more, I promise.

68
00:06:26,552 --> 00:06:27,845
I can't wait anymore.

69
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,223
I wish it were always like this.

70
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:33,476
Peaceful and quiet.

71
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:36,562
Just you and me.

72
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:54,747
[music fades]

73
00:06:57,458 --> 00:07:00,711
-Mom? Mom!
-Lily!

74
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,423
How are you?

75
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:06,551
-I'm okay.
-Were you hurt?

76
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,844
We did it!

77
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:11,472
[uplifting music playing]

78
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,600
Uncle Damian, what happened?

79
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:16,018
Success, Lily.

80
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:18,438
All that's left is ash.

81
00:07:23,317 --> 00:07:25,695
From now on, I'll fight
every battle with you.

82
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:29,699
Thank you.

83
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:33,536
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

84
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:34,912
<i>Please try again later.</i>

85
00:07:36,497 --> 00:07:37,790
I can't reach Jepoy.

86
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:42,086
-Where's Jepoy?
-Custodio?

87
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,338
-Please find Jepoy.
-Yes, sir.

88
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,512
Anna…

89
00:07:52,597 --> 00:07:53,764
We'll find Jepoy.

90
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:59,604
[suspenseful music playing]

91
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:16,370
[door opens]

92
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:19,624
-[glass breaks]
-[screams]

93
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:22,335
Once a liar, always a liar!

94
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:23,211
Even now,

95
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:27,048
you can't keep your promises,
Julio Ardiente!

96
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,925
What are you talking about?!

97
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:30,927
Didn't I get you out of jail?!

98
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:33,513
You also promised me Lily Cruz's head.

99
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:35,306
But look what happened?!

100
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,975
All my money got incinerated!

101
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,478
Well, this would not have happened

102
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:44,148
if you hadn't entrusted Emilia
with your hidden wealth!

103
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:45,525
You see,

104
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:49,278
your daughter is incompetent,
and a nincompoop as well.

105
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,531
Wow! Why are we talking
about me now, Papa?!

106
00:08:51,614 --> 00:08:55,284
Why not? All those booby traps
you set were all defective!

107
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,537
That's the reason why the fire started!

108
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,830
Oh, no! Don't put all the blame on me!

109
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:02,124
We are a team,
and there's no "I" in "team"!

110
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:03,834
Win or lose, we're a team! Duh!

111
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:06,295
Duh! You see? I told you.

112
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,505
She's a nincompoop.

113
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,048
And there's an "I" in "nincompoop"…

114
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:10,967
-…for your information!
-That's your fault!

115
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,927
-How did it become my fault?!
-Enough. Enough.

116
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:14,554
Because you didn't raise her right!

117
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:15,721
-That's enough!
-Just admit that…

118
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,181
-…she took after you!
-My goodness!

119
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:20,226
-I shouldn't have said yes to you!
-Well, then you would've rotted in jail!

120
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:21,852
Enough! You're giving me a migraine!

121
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:23,437
A migraine attack! Enough!

122
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:30,945
We need to drive them out of this town.

123
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:35,741
For good. That way, we can
ensure peace and safety

124
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:37,535
in Poblacion Ardiente.

125
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:41,956
Do you have a plan?

126
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:45,084
I do.

127
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:47,461
But Diego…

128
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:49,422
I want to hear your opinion too.

129
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:52,758
Because we might just pull this off

130
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:54,760
if we really get down to planning it.

131
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,734
[coughs]

132
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:13,946
[groans]

133
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:33,215
[groans]

134
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:36,302
[grunts]

135
00:10:49,231 --> 00:10:51,901
Hello there, Mr. Madrigal!

136
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:55,279
I am Natalia, at your service.

137
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:00,785
Let me go.

138
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:04,372
Not so fast!

139
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,208
I think you're a bit too weak.

140
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:11,712
That's why tonight, you are my master,

141
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:14,507
and I am your slave.

142
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:17,802
Your wish is my command.

143
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:21,347
Leave me alone!

144
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:25,351
Why are you so grumpy?

145
00:11:26,602 --> 00:11:29,897
I already saved your life, yet again.

146
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:34,819
And I think you should just
be grateful that I'm here…

147
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:36,695
to take care of you.

148
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:41,325
-Just rest.
-[groans]

149
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:45,788
And I hate to break it to you, lover boy,

150
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:49,375
but I'm all you've got.

151
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:51,669
I think…

152
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:55,214
you should just accept the fact

153
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:58,259
that it's just you and me.

154
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:06,267
I said…

155
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:10,312
Let me go.

156
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:22,700
That's enough. I'll do it.

157
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:24,452
Where's my stuff?

158
00:12:27,329 --> 00:12:28,372
[groaning]

159
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,464
[groans]

160
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:38,299
-I already told you…
-I'm fine!

161
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:40,134
Don't touch me.

162
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,220
[Jepoy groans]

163
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,725
Where are my things?

164
00:12:48,642 --> 00:12:49,643
Where are they?!

165
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:52,271
Madrigal.

166
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:55,900
Can you just please
let me take care of you?!

167
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:59,111
I don't care if you don't
want to fool around. It's okay!

168
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:01,113
Can you just rest?!

169
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,032
Please!

170
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:04,825
Let me take care of you.

171
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:07,536
[soft music playing]

172
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,662
Please?

173
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:12,875
[Jepoy sighs]

174
00:13:15,085 --> 00:13:16,795
Just… Let's go.

175
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:19,715
Please!

176
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:24,845
Please?

177
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:31,894
[soft music playing]

178
00:13:43,405 --> 00:13:44,406
[groans]

179
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,551
Drink.

180
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:40,754
Anna. Jepoy called.

181
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:42,047
He said he was fine.

182
00:14:42,715 --> 00:14:43,757
Where is he?

183
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:48,262
He didn't say, but he's resting now.

184
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:52,808
Why won't he just come here as planned?

185
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:56,437
Doesn't he realize how worried we are?!

186
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,024
Why does he have to be so selfish?

187
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:08,240
Don't worry, Anna. What's important…

188
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,659
is that he's all right.

189
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:12,202
So, take it easy.

190
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:14,788
Me? Worried?

191
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:18,626
He could never come back, for all I care.

192
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,794
I'm just worried about you
and Auntie Camia.

193
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:23,047
I don't care what he does.

194
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:39,605
Lily… I'll try talking to Anna.

195
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:42,983
Thanks.

196
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:55,412
[knocks on door]

197
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:57,081
Come in.

198
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,667
-Governor.
-Yes?

199
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,126
You have to see this.

200
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:05,965
[tense music playing]

201
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:12,304
[people clamoring]

202
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:16,558
That happened in the next town.
Someone made it rain money.

203
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:18,352
Those poor people!

204
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:21,730
Do you know who's behind this?

205
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:24,191
Someone we already suspected.

206
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:29,822
Ah.

207
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:32,533
My money! My money!

208
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:34,201
-[yelps]
-[tablet thumps]

209
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,456
Our people saw Lily Cruz and Diego Torillo

210
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,500
giving your money away to the people.

211
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,717
Governor, what should we do
to Lily Cruz and Diego Torillo?

212
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:50,968
Shoot them!

213
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:54,013
No. I want to burn them.

214
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,015
I want to burn them alive!

215
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,224
[Julio shushes]

216
00:16:57,307 --> 00:17:00,102
He's asking me,
so I'm the one who'll answer.

217
00:17:00,519 --> 00:17:02,646
And make the final decision, okay?

218
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:05,149
Those two lovebirds hit me where it hurt,

219
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,234
so I'm the one
who should make the decision.

220
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:10,320
And I don't care if your lapdog
will obey me or not.

221
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:11,613
I can do it for myself!

222
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:13,699
Wait for me, Mama!

223
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:17,327
I'll go with her!

224
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:19,747
So…

225
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:22,875
-Governor, what's your plan?
-[shushes]

226
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:25,711
Just get out. Go.

227
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:28,297
Let me have some peace and quiet.

228
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,562
[exhales]

229
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:46,940
[tense music playing]

230
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,530
[soft music playing]

231
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:03,499
Damian, thank you for helping Lily.

232
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,587
You know I'd do anything for you and Lily.

233
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:10,631
But I hope…

234
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:14,551
you'll be more careful next time.

235
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:18,388
-Ouch.
-Oh, sorry. Sorry.

236
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:26,188
[soft music continues playing]

237
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:40,369
Lily.

238
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:51,672
You know how Jepoy and Anna
are more than my friends, right?

239
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:54,925
They're like my siblings.

240
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:57,094
But I'm worried about them.

241
00:18:57,886 --> 00:19:02,432
Just when they finally
professed their love

242
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:03,642
for each other,

243
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,563
that's when they started
hurting each other.

244
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,401
That's how love is.

245
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:15,654
It can bring happiness.

246
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:17,531
It can also bring pain.

247
00:19:19,616 --> 00:19:21,702
But, Lily, not all relationships last.

248
00:19:22,786 --> 00:19:24,538
What matters most is that…

249
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:26,957
they were able to tell
each other how they felt.

250
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:30,335
It's important…

251
00:19:33,046 --> 00:19:36,758
to let the person you love know
just how much you do…

252
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:39,553
before it's too late.

253
00:19:42,639 --> 00:19:43,640
That's why…

254
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,478
I will never get tired of telling you

255
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:55,277
and making you feel
just how much I truly love you.

256
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,326
We don't know what tomorrow might bring,

257
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:04,578
or the day after that.

258
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:10,500
Whatever happens tomorrow
or in the days to come,

259
00:20:10,709 --> 00:20:12,669
there's only one thing I'm sure of.

260
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:15,797
We'll always be together.

261
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:25,682
[soft music playing]

262
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,076
You must be tired, Damian.

263
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:45,994
You should get some rest.

264
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:47,913
I'm not tired.

265
00:20:50,874 --> 00:20:52,501
But I admit I'm getting tired

266
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:54,962
of seeing you avoiding
these moments between us.

267
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:01,468
I love you.

268
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:03,804
[soft music playing]

269
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:06,848
You love me?

270
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:12,854
Damian, I am your brother's wife.

271
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,941
You know everything I've been through.

272
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:17,901
You know--

273
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,157
-You know everything--
-I do!

274
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:25,534
Yes, I do!

275
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:28,996
But that doesn't change
the fact that I love you!

276
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,165
Camia, I'm not perfect.

277
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:34,584
I'm nothing compared to Dante!

278
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:38,171
I might be a criminal,
but I'm telling the truth!

279
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,718
And don't we all deserve to love

280
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,761
and be loved no matter who we might be?

281
00:21:46,555 --> 00:21:48,265
To be loved for who we are.

282
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,690
<i>I'm Damian, by the way.</i>

283
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:01,987
<i>-Oh.</i>
<i>-Oh.</i>

284
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:04,448
<i>Are you all right?</i>

285
00:22:04,531 --> 00:22:06,033
<i>I saw this guy steal your bag.</i>

286
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,626
Camia, I can see it in your eyes.

287
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,462
I know you have feelings for me.

288
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:32,184
Damian…

289
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:37,564
When Dante died, it felt like
a part of me died with him.

290
00:22:38,940 --> 00:22:41,568
So, I don't know
if there's anything left in me.

291
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:46,073
I don't know if I can still love again.

292
00:22:47,491 --> 00:22:48,825
I just don't.

293
00:22:56,208 --> 00:22:59,211
[sad music playing]

294
00:23:05,675 --> 00:23:08,220
All right. I'll go back inside, okay?

295
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,806
Sure, I'll be right in.

296
00:23:19,397 --> 00:23:22,400
[romantic music playing]

297
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:55,809
[romantic music playing]

298
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:07,571
<i>Help!</i>

299
00:24:08,321 --> 00:24:10,323
[young Diego sobs]

300
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:12,409
[young Lily] <i>Hey! Grab my hand!</i>

301
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:13,827
<i>That's it.</i>

302
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:15,453
<i>Slowly! Get up! Careful, come on!</i>

303
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:17,038
<i>My name is Lily.</i>

304
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,999
<i>Mom, Dad, this is Diego.</i>

305
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:22,794
<i>I'll teach you how to lose</i>
<i>weight even if you eat a lot!</i>

306
00:24:44,107 --> 00:24:45,150
<i>Diego.</i>

307
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:52,949
<i>Ivy Aguas.</i>

308
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:19,476
[Diego] <i>I didn't know. I'm sorry.</i>

309
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,978
<i>-How dare you peep at me?!</i>
<i>-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.</i>

310
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:24,606
<i>-Sorry?!</i>
<i>-Ouch! Ow!</i>

311
00:25:24,689 --> 00:25:27,192
<i>-Let them go!</i>
<i>-Loring!</i>

312
00:25:27,859 --> 00:25:29,319
<i>You're hurting them!</i>

313
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:33,865
<i>Let them go!</i>

314
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,200
<i>-Get in!</i>
<i>-Let them go!</i>

315
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:38,828
[romantic music continues playing]

316
00:26:26,793 --> 00:26:28,461
<i>We've been through so much.</i>

317
00:26:29,921 --> 00:26:31,881
<i>And so many people have tried</i>
<i>to come between us.</i>

318
00:26:32,882 --> 00:26:34,134
<i>And yet, here we are…</i>

319
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:36,386
<i>stronger than ever.</i>

320
00:26:37,846 --> 00:26:40,473
<i>Our love is going</i>
<i>to last a lifetime, Lily.</i>

321
00:26:41,808 --> 00:26:42,934
<i>There's no turning back.</i>

322
00:27:02,078 --> 00:27:03,872
<i>I love you so much, Diego.</i>

323
00:27:04,581 --> 00:27:09,127
<i>I couldn't have come this far without you.</i>

324
00:27:10,587 --> 00:27:13,256
<i>I can't wait for all this to be over,</i>

325
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:16,301
<i>so we can finally start</i>
<i>our peaceful lives together</i>

326
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:18,219
<i>as we've always wanted.</i>

327
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,430
[music fades]

328
00:27:22,682 --> 00:27:25,810
[sad music playing]

329
00:27:29,773 --> 00:27:31,816
[Camia sniffles, exhales]

330
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,531
[Camia weeps]

331
00:27:42,786 --> 00:27:45,413
[sobs]

332
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:49,793
Auntie?

333
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,545
Auntie, what's wrong?

334
00:27:56,633 --> 00:27:57,675
Are you all right?

335
00:28:00,303 --> 00:28:01,763
I'm fine, Diego.

336
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,641
I just need to calm myself down
from worrying.

337
00:28:07,435 --> 00:28:09,687
But I can't help it

338
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:13,775
when you, Lily, and the
others go out on these missions.

339
00:28:16,694 --> 00:28:19,322
Auntie, you know we never
go out unprepared.

340
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:23,284
But something can always go wrong, Diego.

341
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:27,705
I know how it feels
to lose the love of your life,

342
00:28:27,789 --> 00:28:30,208
and I don't want any of you
to go through that.

343
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:35,088
I dedicated my life to my husband.

344
00:28:36,965 --> 00:28:38,842
I gave him my heart.

345
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:43,012
I get that, Auntie.

346
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,477
But you've still got love
in your life, you know.

347
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:57,736
When I lost Nanny Loring and Uncle Pandoy…

348
00:29:01,781 --> 00:29:03,324
I lost all hope.

349
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:09,372
I was consumed by anger and fear.

350
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:13,918
But Lily…

351
00:29:15,628 --> 00:29:21,426
She taught me how love
can help heal the pain we feel.

352
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:25,555
But first,

353
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:29,184
we have to be ready to
accept love from other people.

354
00:29:31,519 --> 00:29:33,062
Any moment is the right one…

355
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,190
when we're ready to open our hearts.

356
00:29:38,443 --> 00:29:41,446
[sad music playing]

357
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:05,887
[soft music playing]

358
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,441
Lily.

359
00:30:21,986 --> 00:30:24,447
Uncle Damian, how's your wound?

360
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:27,283
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

361
00:30:27,367 --> 00:30:28,243
It was just a scratch.

362
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:32,580
I've experienced much worse, you know.

363
00:30:33,373 --> 00:30:35,792
Ones that could have killed me.

364
00:30:39,879 --> 00:30:43,174
Thank you for being here for me and Mom.

365
00:30:51,432 --> 00:30:55,019
I--I'll talk to you later,
Auntie. Excuse me.

366
00:30:59,399 --> 00:31:00,483
Diego…

367
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:06,906
is something bothering you?

368
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:15,081
Auntie, I'd like to ask you something.

369
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:19,085
[sighs deeply]

370
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:25,216
I was planning on… giving this to Lily.

371
00:31:27,135 --> 00:31:29,429
I want us to start building
our life together.

372
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:32,807
But…

373
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:35,602
I'll only propose to her
if you give me your blessing.

374
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:42,483
Diego, of course you have my blessing!

375
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:45,653
-Yes, I give you my blessing.
-Auntie.

376
00:31:56,205 --> 00:31:57,790
Auntie. Thank you, Auntie.

377
00:31:58,082 --> 00:31:59,709
I've been planning
on asking Lily to marry me.

378
00:31:59,792 --> 00:32:01,419
I was just looking for the right time.

379
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:03,671
And please don't worry.

380
00:32:04,422 --> 00:32:06,215
I'll never hurt your daughter.

381
00:32:07,216 --> 00:32:08,384
I'll love her.

382
00:32:10,678 --> 00:32:12,138
Anything for Lily.

383
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:14,098
Anything for my daughter.

384
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:18,811
And you're right, Diego.

385
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:24,150
We should open ourselves to love.

386
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:30,031
Thank you, Auntie.

387
00:32:38,373 --> 00:32:40,375
-Please don't cry.
-Too late.

388
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:42,961
-Don't cry.
-I couldn't help it!

389
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:44,712
The ring's beautiful too!

390
00:32:59,018 --> 00:33:00,019
[Damian] You know what, Lily?

391
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:03,690
I suddenly remembered your father.

392
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,735
He was such a kind man.

393
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:09,779
He had a heart of gold…

394
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,323
and solid integrity.

395
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:15,284
Kinda like Superman.

396
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:21,416
<i>Thank you.</i>

397
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:23,710
<i>Thank you…</i>

398
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:26,337
<i>for teaching me how to love again.</i>

399
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:32,719
Oh, Diego.

400
00:33:45,898 --> 00:33:52,030
-[pensive music playing]
-[no audible dialogue]

401
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:01,706
So, what now?

402
00:34:05,251 --> 00:34:06,252
Come with me.

403
00:34:07,128 --> 00:34:08,171
What?

404
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:12,467
-Tomorrow.
-Diego…

405
00:34:13,259 --> 00:34:14,969
Since everything's settled now…

406
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:19,932
maybe I can finally have
my girlfriend all to myself.

407
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:23,519
Why? Where are we going?

408
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:25,688
Are we on a mission?

409
00:34:27,023 --> 00:34:30,985
Are my boyfriend and I… on a mission?

410
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:33,613
I want to take you out to dinner.

411
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:37,658
Hmm…

412
00:34:39,285 --> 00:34:43,372
So, my boyfriend wants to go
on a date with me.

413
00:34:44,707 --> 00:34:45,708
Is that it?

414
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,670
You could say that.

415
00:34:50,379 --> 00:34:52,131
Get straight to the point already.

416
00:34:52,590 --> 00:34:55,093
If you don't, I might just say no.

417
00:34:55,676 --> 00:34:58,888
All right, fine I want
to go out on a date…

418
00:35:00,056 --> 00:35:01,182
with my BL.

419
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:05,228
BL? What's "BL"?

420
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:07,146
Pick one.

421
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:10,233
Baby Lily…

422
00:35:11,943 --> 00:35:13,778
or Baby Love?

423
00:35:14,612 --> 00:35:15,780
Diego!

424
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:19,158
You can't be serious, Diego.

425
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:21,327
Honestly, that's the worst.

426
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:28,709
Baby Love's fine.

427
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:31,712
Baby Love, Baby Love,
I love you, Baby Love…

428
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:32,880
Or maybe--

429
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:35,716
I think Baby Lily sounds cuter.

430
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:38,344
-No, I want Baby Love.
-Okay, Baby Love.

431
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:40,304
Baby Love. Baby Love.

432
00:35:40,763 --> 00:35:43,307
-Go on.
-Tomorrow, okay?

433
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,393
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-Great.

434
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:49,647
I'll miss you.

435
00:35:51,399 --> 00:35:54,026
-Already?
-Yeah.

436
00:36:02,201 --> 00:36:03,202
[Diego] Tell you what…

437
00:36:05,913 --> 00:36:07,081
Baby Love…

438
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:10,668
flowers for you.

439
00:36:11,919 --> 00:36:14,839
Straight from my garden too.

440
00:36:16,465 --> 00:36:18,593
You have to make it up to me tomorrow…

441
00:36:18,676 --> 00:36:19,802
-Baby Love.
-Yes.

442
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:21,012
I'll make it up to you tomorrow.

443
00:36:23,639 --> 00:36:24,640
See you.

444
00:36:30,438 --> 00:36:32,815
Bye. Good night.

445
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:39,238
Camia, I love you.

446
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:42,450
You love me too, so what's the problem?!

447
00:36:45,786 --> 00:36:46,829
Too strong.

448
00:36:56,589 --> 00:36:59,175
Camia, I know I remind you of Dante.

449
00:37:02,303 --> 00:37:03,387
Damian, you idiot.

450
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:05,598
Why would you even mention Dante?

451
00:37:07,266 --> 00:37:08,309
[sighs]

452
00:37:09,435 --> 00:37:10,478
How do I do this…

453
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:18,611
Camia…

454
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:21,822
Camia…

455
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:25,952
[knocks on door]

456
00:37:29,622 --> 00:37:30,581
Damian?

457
00:37:35,586 --> 00:37:37,505
Damian, I'm ready to love again.

458
00:37:40,049 --> 00:37:41,592
I love you too, Damian.

459
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:47,515
[romantic music playing]

460
00:38:03,322 --> 00:38:04,699
Watch your step.

461
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,328
You sure you won't come?

462
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:12,039
It's okay, I have to go.

463
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:14,125
Agent Salonga's waiting for me.

464
00:38:15,042 --> 00:38:16,043
Be careful.

465
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:20,923
-I'll see you later.
-All right.

466
00:38:21,507 --> 00:38:22,425
[Lily chuckle]

467
00:38:22,508 --> 00:38:25,511
[ominous music playing]

468
00:38:27,555 --> 00:38:29,098
-Bye.
-Take care.

469
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:33,436
Sir.

470
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:40,901
[ominous music playing]

471
00:38:52,455 --> 00:38:54,248
-Arnaldo.
-Diego.

472
00:38:54,332 --> 00:38:57,251
-How are you?
-I'm okay. How about you?

473
00:38:57,793 --> 00:38:59,962
-I'm doing fine.
-Good.

474
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:03,674
I just wanted to tell you how…

475
00:39:04,633 --> 00:39:06,719
in these past few days, I realized…

476
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:10,222
how lucky I am because you took me in.

477
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,351
Despite my past,

478
00:39:13,434 --> 00:39:16,145
and despite what my family has done.

479
00:39:17,313 --> 00:39:18,981
So, thank you.

480
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:28,908
Remember, we're always here for you.

481
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,578
That's nice to know. Thank you.

482
00:39:34,121 --> 00:39:36,374
Well, I gotta go.
I've got something to do.

483
00:39:38,084 --> 00:39:39,377
Are you and Lily going somewhere?

484
00:39:41,587 --> 00:39:44,131
-Somewhere special.
-Special?

485
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:48,803
By special, do you mean…

486
00:39:50,429 --> 00:39:51,847
you'll propose to her?

487
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:54,433
[chuckles]

488
00:39:54,850 --> 00:39:56,310
I'll tell you about it tomorrow.

489
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:58,562
-I have to go.
-Sure thing.

490
00:39:58,646 --> 00:39:59,855
-Take care!
-You too!

491
00:40:01,690 --> 00:40:03,359
[tense music swelling]

492
00:40:06,612 --> 00:40:07,738
Proposal.

493
00:40:26,674 --> 00:40:29,844
[soft music playing]

494
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:42,148
Damian, what's this for?

495
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:47,736
I've waited so long for this.

496
00:40:53,951 --> 00:40:54,952
[chuckles softly]

497
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:58,122
Hmm. Where are you going?

498
00:40:58,873 --> 00:41:00,791
Stay here with me.

499
00:41:00,875 --> 00:41:03,794
Damian, I have to make breakfast.

500
00:41:10,801 --> 00:41:11,802
That's all?

501
00:41:12,386 --> 00:41:14,180
Stop it. Yes, that's all.

502
00:41:33,491 --> 00:41:36,827
[ominous music playing]

503
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,955
[reporter] <i>The leader of the group</i>

504
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:42,166
<i>responsible for many crimes</i>
<i>in Metro Manila</i>

505
00:41:42,249 --> 00:41:43,417
<i>calls himself the Jaguar.</i>

506
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:46,712
[Damian] <i>Stealing cars got old real fast.</i>

507
00:41:46,795 --> 00:41:50,090
<i>-I want us to enter smuggling…</i>
<i>-Put your guns down!</i>

508
00:41:50,174 --> 00:41:52,635
-[gunshot]
-[laughs]

509
00:41:52,718 --> 00:41:53,969
[Damian] <i>…kidnapping…</i>

510
00:41:55,054 --> 00:41:56,639
<i>What's this?! What's the meaning of this?!</i>

511
00:41:56,722 --> 00:42:00,059
<i>…and illegal drugs!</i>

512
00:42:00,142 --> 00:42:02,645
<i>Are we going to go against big syndicates?</i>

513
00:42:02,728 --> 00:42:04,855
<i>We'll take them all down.</i>

514
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:07,191
[laughs]

515
00:42:07,274 --> 00:42:08,317
<i>Jaguar.</i>

516
00:42:08,651 --> 00:42:10,653
<i>It's so nice to see you!</i>

517
00:42:10,736 --> 00:42:12,863
<i>It's your service that I want.</i>

518
00:42:12,947 --> 00:42:14,240
<i>Answer me, Damian!</i>

519
00:42:14,323 --> 00:42:16,909
<i>Are you part of Red Dragon's syndicate?</i>

520
00:42:18,202 --> 00:42:19,203
<i>No.</i>

521
00:42:23,499 --> 00:42:25,876
<i>I can't keep my secret</i>
<i>from Camia any longer.</i>

522
00:42:27,127 --> 00:42:30,130
[ominous music playing]

523
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:58,617
[tense music playing]

524
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:06,375
Sorry we didn't get to
help you out sooner, Romulo.

525
00:43:07,001 --> 00:43:09,211
It's all right. I got used to it.

526
00:43:10,504 --> 00:43:12,423
Mama and I have a job for you.

527
00:43:14,216 --> 00:43:15,217
Let's go.

528
00:43:27,354 --> 00:43:30,399
[soft music playing]

529
00:43:33,569 --> 00:43:35,029
<i>This is what I've always dreamed of…</i>

530
00:43:36,238 --> 00:43:38,157
<i>A peaceful life with Camia by my side.</i>

531
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:41,076
<i>But it'll never really happen</i>

532
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,745
<i>as long as I work for Red Dragon.</i>

533
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:47,833
Damian.

534
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:50,961
What are you doing? Come here,
and join me for breakfast.

535
00:43:52,046 --> 00:43:53,130
Wow, that looks good!

536
00:44:03,349 --> 00:44:04,391
Excuse me.

537
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:12,816
[Damian] It's time for breakfast.

538
00:44:13,275 --> 00:44:15,361
So, what are you waiting for? Have a seat.

539
00:44:24,328 --> 00:44:25,329
Um…

540
00:44:27,206 --> 00:44:30,751
I've got to take care
of something at work later.

541
00:44:31,335 --> 00:44:35,047
-Mm-hm.
-After that, maybe…

542
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:37,341
we can go out on a date.

543
00:44:38,926 --> 00:44:39,927
What?

544
00:44:40,386 --> 00:44:42,221
If you're not busy, maybe we can…

545
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,182
go out on a date.

546
00:44:47,935 --> 00:44:49,144
Oh, Damian.

547
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:51,814
You're so silly.

548
00:44:51,897 --> 00:44:55,234
We're not teenagers anymore.
We're too old for dates.

549
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:57,736
But I'm not trying to be silly.

550
00:44:58,278 --> 00:45:03,283
Camia, I'm serious. Please?
Let's go out on a date.

551
00:45:03,784 --> 00:45:05,828
I've waited decades to ask you out.

552
00:45:08,789 --> 00:45:09,623
I don't want to. Damian.

553
00:45:23,095 --> 00:45:24,138
Psst.

554
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:29,309
Psst. [chuckles]

555
00:45:31,019 --> 00:45:33,856
Okay. Let's go out.

556
00:45:35,774 --> 00:45:38,068
-Come again?
-Let's go on a date.

557
00:45:38,152 --> 00:45:39,278
-Really?
-Yeah.

558
00:45:45,993 --> 00:45:46,952
Can I taste your apple?

559
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:50,122
That was my hand!

560
00:45:53,333 --> 00:45:54,710
You'll enjoy this date.

561
00:45:55,461 --> 00:45:56,712
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

562
00:45:58,255 --> 00:45:59,214
If you say so.

563
00:46:21,612 --> 00:46:22,654
Look.

564
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:28,285
Can we forget about
that brouhaha the other night?

565
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:32,831
Nothing good will come from
fighting and pointing fingers.

566
00:46:33,999 --> 00:46:34,875
Right?

567
00:46:36,877 --> 00:46:38,253
Listen to me, Helena.

568
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:44,801
Before Lily Cruz came into our lives,

569
00:46:45,719 --> 00:46:49,056
we Ardientes ruled this place
with an iron grip.

570
00:46:51,099 --> 00:46:54,436
Not only because we are rich and powerful,

571
00:46:55,354 --> 00:46:57,564
but because we had one secret.

572
00:46:58,273 --> 00:47:02,528
We had one thing that was
working for us beautifully,

573
00:47:03,153 --> 00:47:06,240
and that is because our family was united,

574
00:47:06,323 --> 00:47:07,533
ready to help one another.

575
00:47:08,951 --> 00:47:11,328
That's why we got everything we wanted.

576
00:47:11,912 --> 00:47:17,376
Of course, we had money and power too.

577
00:47:18,502 --> 00:47:19,753
And we…

578
00:47:20,629 --> 00:47:23,048
we had it all.

579
00:47:25,259 --> 00:47:27,052
Now didn't we, Emilia?

580
00:47:28,178 --> 00:47:30,305
[sighs] Oh, how I miss those days.

581
00:47:31,223 --> 00:47:32,224
Well…

582
00:47:33,183 --> 00:47:36,311
We can relive them again.

583
00:47:37,563 --> 00:47:42,192
That's if you grant my request.

584
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:47,197
To follow you?

585
00:47:48,490 --> 00:47:50,158
No, Helena!

586
00:47:55,539 --> 00:47:59,251
I will help you crush Lily Cruz.

587
00:48:02,379 --> 00:48:06,008
And in the way you want it to happen.

588
00:48:06,091 --> 00:48:07,384
You're the boss.

589
00:48:08,802 --> 00:48:10,721
We'll have it your way.

590
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:13,056
Your way will be followed, okay?

591
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:18,353
We can fulfill your fantasy
about Lily Cruz.

592
00:48:19,354 --> 00:48:22,274
But the only catch is,

593
00:48:23,650 --> 00:48:25,152
we have to help each other.

594
00:48:37,914 --> 00:48:40,000
Oh, come here. Come here.

595
00:48:43,462 --> 00:48:46,506
Oh… Oh!

596
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:51,386
I love my family! Group hug!

597
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:53,764
I love you, Mama! I love you, Papa!

598
00:48:54,514 --> 00:48:55,557
Enough, Papa.

599
00:48:56,016 --> 00:48:57,059
-What?
-Just hug.

600
00:48:57,309 --> 00:49:00,145
-Ju--
-Not the kiss part! Ew!

601
00:49:00,479 --> 00:49:03,231
[pensive music swelling]

602
00:49:06,985 --> 00:49:09,571
[suspenseful music]

603
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:20,332
<i>Tell Madam Red Dragon to start</i>
<i>looking for my replacement.</i>

604
00:49:20,415 --> 00:49:23,877
<i>This isn't the life</i>
<i>I want for my loved ones.</i>

605
00:49:23,960 --> 00:49:25,170
<i>I don't want to be the Jaguar.</i>

606
00:49:25,253 --> 00:49:26,880
[Diego] <i>We don't have</i>
<i>any control over the future.</i>

607
00:49:26,963 --> 00:49:28,840
<i>But we have tonight.</i>

608
00:49:28,924 --> 00:49:32,469
<i>I want to spend the rest</i>
<i>of my life with my best friend.</i>

609
00:49:32,552 --> 00:49:33,595
<i>Will you marry me?</i>

610
00:49:35,806 --> 00:49:38,058
<i>I'm the Jaguar. I worked for Red Dragon.</i>

611
00:49:40,435 --> 00:49:43,939
[Helena] <i>I'm going to take both</i>
<i>of you out of your misery.</i>

612
00:49:45,482 --> 00:49:46,692
<i>Get down!</i>

613
00:49:46,775 --> 00:49:49,569
[gunfire]

614
00:49:49,653 --> 00:49:52,698
[theme music playing]
